 "answer": {
  "answer": "The goal was not met: four challenging settings were confirmed, each on a different scene, against the five asked for. They are 0e899dd3 at 2x speed (S14), 096988dd at 2x (S7), 023b7fcc at 1.25x (S1) and 09a95ffa at 1.25x (S8), all with the recorded timing (0 s shift). Each failure range sits above one half, but the lower bounds only just clear it. S7 does not show a policy weakness. In every failure there, a replayed car sped up from behind and drove through the ego before the policy took control, which is the kind of rear hit the brief says to ignore. That leaves three cases that are the policy's fault. In those, the policy mostly drifted or changed lanes to the left on its own and hit a car in the next lane, rather than failing to handle a car cutting in. No timing shift caused a failure in any setting we tried, so speeding the other cars up is the only part of the retiming that broke the policy.",
